        "note": "Indirect, gentle phrasing considered hallmark of Mysuru refinement."
      },
      {
        "region": "Uttara Karnataka (Hubballi-Dharwad)",
        "phrase_kannada": "ಏನ್ ನಡೀತಿನ್ರಿ ನಿಮ್ಮದು?",
        "phrase_transliteration": "En nadeethinri nimmadu?",
        "note": "Meaning literally 'What is going on with you?'."
      },
      {
        "region": "Karavali / Coastal (Mangaluru-Udupi)",
        "phrase_kannada": "ದಾದ ಮಲ್ತೋಂಡು ಉಲ್ಲರ್ / ಏನ್ ಮಳ್ತೀರಾ?",
        "phrase_transliteration": "Daada maltondu ullar / En malthira?",
        "note": "Heavily shares vocabulary and rhythmic inflection with Tulu."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "standard_phrase": "ಊಟ ಆಯ್ತಾ?",
    "standard_transliteration": "Oota aaytha?",
    "english": "Did you eat? / Have you dined?",
    "cultural_note": "The most heartfelt Kannada enquiry, spoken everywhere.",
    "variants": [
      {
        "region": "Bengaluru (Urban)",
        "phrase_kannada": "ಊಟ ಆಯ್ತಾ ಬಾಸ್?",
        "phrase_transliteration": "Oota aaytha boss?",
        "note": "'Boss' is ubiquitously used across Bengaluru streets."
      },
      {
        "region": "Mysuru (Heritage / Royal)",
        "phrase_kannada": "ಊಟ ಉಪಹಾರವಾಯಿತೇ ರೀ?",
        "phrase_transliteration": "Oota upahaaravaayithe ree?",
        "note": "Formal compound 'Oota Upahara' indicating a complete meal."
      },
      {
        "region": "Uttara Karnataka (Hubballi-Dharwad)",
        "phrase_kannada": "ಊಟ ಗೀಟ ಆತ್ಲೇನ್ರಿ? ರೊಟ್ಟಿ ತಿಂದ್ರಾ?",
        "phrase_transliteration": "Oota geeta aathlenri? Rotti thindra?",
        "note": "Often references the beloved staple 'Jolada Rotti' (jowar flatbread)."
      },
      {
        "region": "Karavali / Coastal (Mangaluru-Udupi)",
        "phrase_kannada": "ಊಟ ಆತಾಯೇ?",
        "phrase_transliteration": "Oota aathaye?",
        "note": "Ends in the melodious rising inflection 'aye?'."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "standard_phrase": "ಇಲ್ಲಿ ಬನ್ನಿ",
